Don't allocate a Bukkit Vector for entity pushes nothing observes.

Entity#push(double, double, double, Entity) built an org.bukkit.util.Vector on every call, before
checking whether anything would use it. Ordinary entity-vs-entity crowding goes through the
pushingEntity == null path, where the Vector was constructed only to be unpacked straight back into
three doubles.

EntityPushedByEntityAttackEvent was also fired unguarded. It can only cancel the push or replace
the knockback, so with no listener registered the raw xa/ya/za are what end up applied either way -
skipping the event is exactly equivalent.

push() runs for every entity being shoved by another, every tick, so this is one of the hotter
allocation sites on a crowded server.

--- a/leaf-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java
+++ b/leaf-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java
@@ -2604,11 +2604,26 @@
-            org.bukkit.util.Vector delta = new org.bukkit.util.Vector(xa, ya, za);
-            if (pushingEntity != null) {
-                EntityPushedByEntityAttackEvent event = new EntityPushedByEntityAttackEvent(this.getBukkitEntity(), Cause.PUSH, pushingEntity.getBukkitEntity(), delta);
-                if (!event.callEvent()) return;
-                delta = event.getKnockback();
-            }
-            this.setDeltaMovement(this.getDeltaMovement().add(delta.getX(), delta.getY(), delta.getZ()));
+            double pushX = xa;
+            double pushY = ya;
+            double pushZ = za;
+            if (pushingEntity != null
+                && EntityPushedByEntityAttackEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length != 0) {
+                org.bukkit.util.Vector delta = new org.bukkit.util.Vector(xa, ya, za);
+                EntityPushedByEntityAttackEvent event = new EntityPushedByEntityAttackEvent(this.getBukkitEntity(), Cause.PUSH, pushingEntity.getBukkitEntity(), delta);
+                if (!event.callEvent()) return;
+                delta = event.getKnockback();
+                pushX = delta.getX();
+                pushY = delta.getY();
+                pushZ = delta.getZ();
+            }
+            this.setDeltaMovement(this.getDeltaMovement().add(pushX, pushY, pushZ));
